    "message": {
     "content": "**Yes, you should strongly lean toward taking this offer.** \n\nGetting a **$200,000 sign-on bonus** alongside a base match ($240,000) and $1.08M in equity makes this a top-tier package for a Google L6 Product Manager. It completely changes the financial equation from a lateral move to a substantial windfall.\n\n---\n\n### The Numbers: How Your Compensation Looks Now\n\n#### Year 1 Total Compensation: **~$758,000 \u2013 $844,000+**\n\n* **Base:** $240,000\n* **Target Bonus (20%):** $48,000\n* **Sign-On Bonus:** $200,000\n* **Year 1 Equity Vest:**\n  * *If flat vesting (25%/yr):* $270,000 $\\rightarrow$ **Total Year 1 = $758,000**\n  * *If Google standard front-loaded (e.g., 33% / 33% / 22% / 12%):* $356,400 $\\rightarrow$ **Total Year 1 = $844,400**\n\n#### Years 2\u20134 Baseline: **~$558,000+/year** (Excluding Refreshes)\nEven after the sign-on bonus drops off, your baseline recurring comp ($240k base + $48k bonus + $270k avg equity) exceeds your current $526k run rate at Meta, before adding annual equity refresh grants.\n\n---\n\n### Why This Is Such a Strong Win\n\n1. **You fully liquidated your transition risk:** By giving you $200k in cash, Google effectively bought out the exact dollar value of the unvested Meta RSUs you would walk away from over the next 12 months. You get that value *plus* your new Google equity vesting in parallel.\n2. **Top-of-Band Sign-On:** For an L6 at Google, sign-on bonuses typically top out around $75k\u2013$120k. Securing $200k is an exceptional outcome that compensation committees rarely approve without strong executive support.\n3. **Resetting Your Equity Clock:** You lock in a fresh $1.08M 4-year grant at today\u2019s grant price.\n\n---\n\n### 3 Things to Verify Before Signing\n\n1. **Sign-On Payout & Clawback Terms:**\n   * Clarify whether the $200k is paid out in one lump sum (typically within your first 1\u20132 paychecks) or split across Year 1 and Year 2.\n   * Check the repayment/clawback clause (usually 1 year, prorated if you leave early).\n2. **Exact Vesting Schedule:**\n   * Confirm if the $1.08M vests monthly over 4 years on a flat schedule (25% per year) or on Google's front-loaded schedule (e.g., 33%/33%/22%/12%). A front-loaded schedule makes Year 1 & 2 even richer.\n3. **Start Date Timing vs. Meta Vesting/Bonus:**\n   * Look at Meta's next vesting date and bonus payout date. If you are just a few weeks away from a quarterly vest, set your Google start date immediately after that vest so you capture both.\n\n---\n\n### Final Verdict\n\nUnless you have severe concerns about the specific product area, your future manager, or Google\u2019s product culture compared to Meta\u2019s, **this is an offer you should accept.** You maximized your leverage and turned a lateral offer into a ~$230k\u2013$310k+ Year 1 premium.",
